    <title>Django: Ticket #34384: SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS is not used for sessions</title>
    <link>https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/34384</link>
    <description>&lt;p&gt;
I recently rotated my secret key, made the old one available in &lt;code&gt;SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS&lt;/code&gt; and I&#39;m pretty sure everyone on our site is logged out now.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
I think the docs for &lt;a class=&#34;ext-link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/4.1/ref/settings/#secret-key-fallbacks&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;icon&#34;&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS&lt;/a&gt; may be incorrect when stating the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
In order to rotate your secret keys, set a new SECRET_KEY and move the previous value to the beginning of SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS. Then remove the old values from the end of the SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS when you are ready to expire the sessions, password reset tokens, and so on, that make use of them.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
When looking at the Django source code, I see that the &lt;a class=&#34;ext-link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/django/django/blob/4.1.7/django/utils/crypto.py#L19-L45&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;icon&#34;&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;salted_hmac&lt;/a&gt; function uses the &lt;code&gt;SECRET_KEY&lt;/code&gt; by default and the &lt;a class=&#34;ext-link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/django/django/blob/4.1.7/django/contrib/auth/base_user.py#L127-L136&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;icon&#34;&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;AbstractBaseUser.get_session_auth_hash&lt;/a&gt; method does not call &lt;code&gt;salted_hmac&lt;/code&gt; with a value for the &lt;code&gt;secret&lt;/code&gt; keyword argument.
&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
