    <item>

      <dc:creator>Joey Lange</dc:creator>
      <pubDate>Fri, 03 Mar 2023 20:33:10 GMT</pubDate>
      <title>cc changed</title>
      <link>https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/34384#comment:3      </link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/34384#comment:3</guid>
      <description>
        &lt;ul&gt;
          &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;cc&lt;/strong&gt;
        &lt;span class=&#34;trac-author&#34;&gt;Joey Lange&lt;/span&gt; added
          &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
Hi! I&#39;m a colleague of Eric&#39;s, and we were discussing some of the ramifications of fixing this issue and I thought I&#39;d write them here for posterity.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
In particular for user sessions, using fallback keys in the &lt;code&gt;AuthenticationMiddleware&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;auth.get_user(request)&lt;/code&gt; will keep existing &lt;code&gt;_auth_user_hash&lt;/code&gt; values from before the rotation being seen as valid, which is nice during the rotation period, but without any &lt;em&gt;upgrading&lt;/em&gt; of the &lt;code&gt;_auth_user_hash&lt;/code&gt; values, when the rotation is finished and the fallback keys are removed, all of those sessions will essentially be invalidated again.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
So, I think possibly an additional need here is a way to upgrade the cookies when a fallback key is used? Or at least documentation calling out this drawback.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
Edit: It&#39;s possible I&#39;m conflating a cookie value and a session value, but either way I think the principle of what I wrote stands?
&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
      <category>Ticket</category>
    </item>
    <item>

      <dc:creator>Mariusz Felisiak</dc:creator>
      <pubDate>Mon, 06 Mar 2023 08:00:37 GMT</pubDate>
      <title>cc, severity, stage changed</title>
      <link>https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/34384#comment:4      </link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/34384#comment:4</guid>
      <description>
        &lt;ul&gt;
          &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;cc&lt;/strong&gt;
        &lt;span class=&#34;trac-author&#34;&gt;Carlton Gibson&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;trac-author&#34;&gt;Andreas Pelme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;trac-author&#34;&gt;terrameijar&lt;/span&gt; added
          &lt;/li&gt;
          &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;severity&lt;/strong&gt;
        &lt;span class=&#34;trac-field-old&#34;&gt;Normal&lt;/span&gt; → &lt;span class=&#34;trac-field-new&#34;&gt;Release blocker&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;/li&gt;
          &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;stage&lt;/strong&gt;
        &lt;span class=&#34;trac-field-old&#34;&gt;Unreviewed&lt;/span&gt; → &lt;span class=&#34;trac-field-new&#34;&gt;Accepted&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
Thanks for the report. Agreed, we should check fallback session hashes.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
Bug in &lt;a class=&#34;changeset&#34; href=&#34;https://code.djangoproject.com/changeset/0dcd549bbe36c060f536ec270d34d9e7d4b8e6c7/&#34; title=&#34;Fixed #30360 -- Added support for secret key rotation.

Thanks Florian ...&#34;&gt;0dcd549bbe36c060f536ec270d34d9e7d4b8e6c7&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote class=&#34;citation&#34;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
In particular for user sessions, using fallback keys in the &lt;code&gt;AuthenticationMiddleware&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;auth.get_user(request)&lt;/code&gt; will keep existing &lt;code&gt;_auth_user_hash&lt;/code&gt; values from before the rotation being seen as valid, which is nice during the rotation period, but without any upgrading of the &lt;code&gt;_auth_user_hash&lt;/code&gt; values, when the rotation is finished and the fallback keys are removed, all of those sessions will essentially be invalidated again.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
So, I think possibly an additional need here is a way to upgrade the cookies when a fallback key is used? Or at least documentation calling out this drawback.
Edit: It&#39;s possible I&#39;m conflating a cookie value and a session value, but either way I think the principle of what I wrote stands?
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
As far as I&#39;m aware, this is a new feature request not a bug in &lt;a class=&#34;closed ticket&#34; href=&#34;https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/30360&#34; title=&#34;#30360: New feature: Support rotation of secret keys. (closed: fixed)&#34;&gt;#30360&lt;/a&gt;, so we should discuss it separately. Maybe we could call &lt;code&gt;update_session_auth_hash()&lt;/code&gt; when a fallback hash is valid 🤔 
&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
      <category>Ticket</category>
    </item>
